14: // ── 0B (2026-09-02) — BE+40 AND THE ATR TRAIL ARE SUSPENDED ─────────────────
15: //
16: // Both mechanisms are LIVE and FIRING (full audit 09-01: 2 breakeven moves, 8
17: // trail ratchets that day) with NO measurement of whether they help. Round-7
18: // research ranks ATR/Chandelier trails in the worst group of 15 exit families
19: // across 567,000 backtests, and the net effect of breakeven moves is contested.
20: // Our own tape shows $719.50 of giveback with ZERO trail EXITS ever recorded.
21: //
22: // The problem is not the direction of the effect — it is that unmeasured
23: // mechanisms are moving live stops. Suspended (not deleted) until MFE data
24: // exists (wave 1A). Exits while suspended: fixed stop · fixed target · EOD flat
25: // · the existing invalidation/dormant logic.
26: //
27: // Env EXIT_MECHS_SUSPENDED=0 re-enables both (the knobs are retained; per-
28: // strategy breakeven_enabled / trailing_enabled still gate them underneath).
29:
30: // ExitMechSuspendedLabel is the one-line reason shown in logs and the Guide.
31: const ExitMechSuspendedLabel = "suspended 2026-09-02 pending MFE data (wave 1A)"
32:
33: // exitMechsSuspended resolves the suspension (env EXIT_MECHS_SUSPENDED,
34: // default TRUE = suspended).
35: func exitMechsSuspended() bool {
36: 	if v := strings.TrimSpace(os.Getenv("EXIT_MECHS_SUSPENDED")); v != "" {
37: 		switch strings.ToLower(v) {
38: 		case "0", "false", "off", "no":
39: 			return false
40: 		}
41: 	}
42: 	return true
43: }
